 that fails loudly instead of silently continuing when the chosen scratch root already holds another lane's live state. Prove with a two-lane dry run on one host: lane A holds a scratch + agent, lane B starts, and lane B either picks a distinct path/port or aborts with the collision named — and lane A's evidence file is intact afterwards.", "reasoning": "Observed live during this tick (2026-10-27, duckbrain dogfood). (1) SCRATCH COLLISION: this lane created /tmp/df-dkb-1027/{root,evidence,logs} at 15:36 local; at ~15:40 the directory was replaced by ANOTHER Hermes session's duckbrain scratch (config.json with namespacesPath=/tmp/df-dkb-1027/namespaces, auth.json {apiKeys:[]}, home/, namespaces/), deleting this lane's evidence dir and its daemon's namespace root (the daemon then served 503 because its root was gone). The other session's daemon /proc environ shows HOME=/tmp/df-dkb-1027/own/home, PWD=/home/kara/duckbrain, HERMES_SESSION_CHAT_ID=b8f5c876-366a-4732-b540-05d8236dc5a5, and it left cli-remember.txt, cli-recall.txt, health-1..5.json, remember-help.txt, search-help.txt, status-help.txt, consolidate.txt, prod-health.json — a second dogfood-style delivery of the SAME project choosing the SAME date-based path convention (/tmp/df-dkb-<MMDD>). (2) PORT COLLISION: this lane's second daemon died at startup with `errno: -98, syscall: 'listen', address: '127.0.0.1', port: 3137` (daemon.log) because the other session had already bound 3137 with `node /home/kara/duckbrain/bin/duckbrain.js http --port=3137 --auth=none` (pid 11576, started 15:43:17 from the systemd --user manager); part of this lane's first confirmation pass was therefore answered by the OTHER session's daemon. (3) AGENT LOSS: this lane launched install agent 0908094c @ bunker-mvp at 20:40:31Z (battery began; cells repo-head/toolchain-bootstrap/fresh-install all OK). The other session captured that agent's evidence to /tmp/df-dkb-1027/install-agent-capture.txt at 15:45 and ran `bunker list --status all` at 15:44:35; by 15:53 `bunker info --server bunker-mvp 0908094c` answered `not_found: agent \"0908094c\" not found` and the agent was absent from `bunker list --status all`, i.e. the leg was destroyed before its Phase-B collection — the ci-pass/native/ui-probe/chaos cells are unrecoverable, and this lane did not destroy it. Demanded fix is the convention + ownership marker above; the immediate mitigation this lane applied was moving its scratch to /home/kara/dfdkb-tick-20261027-2029 (per-run unique) and switching to port 3199. Evidence: journal 15:40:10 systemd entries; /tmp/df-dkb-1027/config.json; /proc/11576/environ; /home/kara/dfdkb-tick-20261027-2029/logs/daemon.log; /home/kara/dfdkb-tick-20261027-2029/evidence/agent-evidence-raw.txt; /tmp/df-dkb-1027/install-agent-capture.txt.", "source": "dogfood", "created_by": "dogfood-duckbrain-2026-10-27", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:02:02.000000+00:00", "ts": "2026-10-27T21:02:02.000000+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-03 02:29:18", "blocked_reason": "lane-infra, not duckbrain repo source: the deliverable (per-run-unique scratch root + port, install-agent ownership marker, pre-spawn deconfliction probe) lives in the dogfood lane's scripts under ~/.hermes/scripts/ and its lane spec, so no worker in this repo can land it.", "foreman_note": "Carried forward from the 01-18-22 wave manifest's deferral — re-confirmed this tick after DF-2026-5/6/8/9 landed. Needs a lane-level task (dogfood lane), not a duckbrain worker.", "worker_status": "dispatched", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/duckbrain-DF-2026-7", "branch": "wt/DF-2026-7"}
 {"id": "DF-2026-8", "status": "complete", "priority": "P5", "title": "P5 — docs/reality drift on the HTTP API reference: tombstoned versions are absent from the list even with historical=true, and GET /mcp is documented as a supported route while it answers 405", "acceptance_criteria": "Correct docs/api/http-api.md to match the shipped behaviour (or change the behaviour to match the doc, whichever the spec owner rules). Specifically: (a) the same-key multi-version note says 'the list route returns all of them' and the historical=true filter says it includes ALL rows regardless of validity window — state explicitly that tombstoned versions are excluded from both views, OR return them; (b) the MCP transport section advertises `GET /mcp` while the daemon answers 405 'this endpoint does not offer a GET SSE stream' — either describe GET as status-only/unavailable or implement it. Prove with a live daemon: create a memory, DELETE it, then GET /api/memories?prefix=<key>&historical=true and GET /mcp; quote both responses in the row and in the doc's own wording.", "acceptance": "Correct docs/api/http-api.md to match the shipped behaviour (or change the behaviour to match the doc, whichever the spec owner rules). Specifically: (a) the same-key multi-version note says 'the list route returns all of them' and the historical=true filter says it includes ALL rows regardless of validity window — state explicitly that tombstoned versions are excluded from both views, OR return them; (b) the MCP transport section advertises `GET /mcp` while the daemon answers 405 'this endpoint does not offer a GET SSE stream' — either describe GET as status-only/unavailable or implement it. Prove with a live daemon: create a memory, DELETE it, then GET /api/memories?prefix=<key>&historical=true and GET /mcp; quote both responses in the row and in the doc's own wording.", "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-10-27 (tick duckbrain-dogfood-2026-10-27-20-29-19), HEAD db695496, isolated scratch daemons (ports 3199 and 3137), same result on both. (a) TOMBSTONES: wrote /quickstart/victim, then `curl -X DELETE .../api/memories/<id>?namespace=quickstart` -> 204; the namespace storage still holds the tombstone row (grep -c tombstone namespaces/quickstart/concept/*/current.jsonl = 1; the row carries action 'tombstone' with the same key), yet `GET /api/memories?namespace=quickstart&prefix=/quickstart/victim&historical=true` -> `{\"items\":[],\"total\":0,...}` and the plain list is empty too. docs/api/http-api.md (Memories note) says 'GET /api/memories/key/:key returns the most recent non-tombstoned version, while the list route returns all of them', and the `historical` param is documented as 'true = historical view including ALL rows regardless of validity window'. A client that forgets and then audits the list cannot see that the version existed. (b) GET /mcp: docs/api/http-api.md 'MCP Transport' documents `POST /mcp` AND `GET /mcp`; live `curl -H 'X-API-Key: ***' http://127.0.0.1:3199/mcp` -> HTTP 405 `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"error\":{\"code\":-32000,\"message\":\"Method Not Allowed: this endpoint does not offer a GET SSE stream\"}}`. The 406-without-Accept and 200-with-Accept POST legs do match the doc exactly (tools/list returned 16 tools: recall, remember, list_keys, forget, squash, get_compaction_stats, create_namespace, list_namespaces, switch_namespace, delete_namespace, server_status, server_http_start, list_profiles, create_profile, update_profile, select_profiles). Evidence: /home/kara/dfdkb-tick-20261027-2029/evidence/confirm.txt + conf-tomb-hist.json + conf-mcp-get.json.", "source": "dogfood", "created_by": "dogfood-duckbrain-2026-10-27", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:02:03.000000+00:00", "ts": "2026-10-27T21:02:03.000000+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-27T21:02:03.000000+00:00", "commit_hash": "9d270dea1620bb6dfa8ded5f72e4bea12e60ce85", "worker_status": "complete", "branch": "wt/DF-2026-8", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/duckbrain-DF-2026-8 (merged, reaped)", "file