 {"id": "TESTQ-2026-11-02-1", "title": "P2 CI red on main: tests/http-ratelimit.int.test.ts third test receives HTTP 429 from the daemon it started with --rate-limit=100 (run 41453591399, sha e9c44120)", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:05:00Z", "created_by": "duckbrain-ci-test-quality-audit cron", "complexity": 2, "detail": {"fingerprint": "3bee2dd82ee092014bf066d9d43faa2d976e660eee6f0394384800fe67db8df2", "evidence": [{"run_id": "41453591399", "ts": "2026-11-02T13:30:39Z", "sha": "e9c44120f2ec2ca7dfb775cb75a295c41e55c548"}]}, "reasoning": "GitHub run 41453591399 (main, sha e9c44120 'qa-cron: 2026-11-02 findings', a board-only commit: tasks.jsonl +1) failed step 'Run integration tests' with 1 failed / 82 passed / 1 skipped. Failing block: tests/http-ratelimit.int.test.ts:66 \"AssertionError: expected [ 200, 503 ] to include 429\" (Vitest prints it reversed: the RECEIVED status was 429) in 'should include X-RateLimit-Limit header on successful requests', test duration 12156ms. That test spawns its OWN daemon on a fresh getRandomPort() with rateLimit 100 and waits for /health; a fresh token bucket at 100/min cannot return 429 inside ~12s (the readiness poller runs one curl per ~200ms, all of them connection-refused until the port answers), so the 429 was answered by a listener whose bucket was ALREADY empty - not the child. 12156ms is ~the 12s refill interval of limit 5/min, the budget of the FIRST describe's daemon (startDuckbrainHttp rateLimit 5) exhausted by the preceding 'should return 429 after exceeding rate limit' test: after ~12s one token refilled, waitForUrl accepted that 200, and the test's own request then found the bucket empty. So the third test was talking to a port another daemon owned (reused/leaked port) and the harness never noticed: startDuckbrainHttp does not surface a child that exits on EADDRINUSE, getRandomPort does not probe the port, and nothing asserts the listener is the child just spawned. NOT the closed INT-CI-003 class (that was a waitForUrl timeout on this same file), NOT RATE-LIMIT-001 (product 429 logging, landed), NOT count drift or a runner block. REPRO of the shape: start a daemon with --rate-limit=5 on port P, burn >5 GET /health until 429, then run the third test body against P: it returns 200 after ~12s in waitForUrl and the next request gets 429 exactly as in CI. Current tree: 'CI=true npx vitest run --config vitest.integration.config.ts tests/http-ratelimit.int.test.ts' = 3/3 in 2.7s locally, and run 41404266474 (07:07Z) was green, so this is a race, not a deterministic break. FIX: (1) startDuckbrainHttp rejects loudly when the child exits before its port answers, quoting the child stderr tail; (2) getRandomPort returns a port proven bindable right before use; (3) the readiness probe must not consume the limiter under test - use a separate bypass path or a per-spawn nonce header/X-RateLimit-Limit assert - so the test proves it is talking to its own child (X-RateLimit-Limit must equal the configured limit and the status follow). ACCEPTANCE: 10 consecutive 'CI=true pnpm test:integration' runs with zero 429 in this file, plus the next integration CI job green on the fix commit; do not weaken the 429 assertion in the second test.", "updated_at": "2026-11-02T14:05:00Z"}
